    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-21632",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/4b782a37c2e75edce01f6cc4204b8460eeeddfcda6c9a19e71d457f2d26c9e37.svg)\nSketch the phase portrait of the system of linear differential equations above, given that the eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/e2c67900a3ba263aad1f200c892be4d755ab441e6b96ad6317e9364121f597b4.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/13ce986fa0d524d648d9ef04a684f3ea8f4a461551dc752a637421a892d6ab78.svg) for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/6909fb833286a13cf8c6c5bb40fde4090215e21536551aa1fa8ccac3b7d5ed65.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/25ea6517999dfc2d7a84ff6ef0010ede0633c32b9673882d3ddf8535c4b140e8.svg) respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution of the system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/bc65e04739f9a5ad34beeec6de1529e1ccecac090950e501d7eddda68b0a6c6d.svg)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/ae627e517d44488fe9878a28529140cc256eade4aadfe0445c8945ff066398ba.svg) has the equation \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/39e03f3df5d6dd4a54b575a823498cda07cbe15e21e05a9cde5e0ad900def247.svg)\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/966a241524851dd38dc511f730fa023c3b2755f67a7fb1f6476ef4caf083ba94.svg)\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/def1e6afa80a61af78e69da17bdf65200185f760454a98ffa8b56142cd99b08f.svg) as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/3a4f4cfc9409e86d8918647d161f6cccccd1ba270e603575b8fc9f5167e58a48.svg) these solutions approach the origin as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg)\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/ff535f17581c5a93045c3c23b8b33ca2996be6dfca63ed7808bc5fec809d2377.png)\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/d57858ae72e3b836de8c930917b65bcfef13cd3b85518933523024f84905a05b.svg) has the equation \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/8f96aa73ce843c7815a1fed6bf3f3774a173cfa4d56f13e1f3a8c48d53cd7097.svg)\nand the straight-line solutions of the form\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/b2a991e2b459a17fc02d58d3eb267f04c03d03f8224561bc234513aa5dfc8a7a.svg)\nlie on that line. \n\nSince ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/b2e3de236be1367c614d785fd065d91340a14b9197fb77734c537161645f69ba.svg) as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/3a4f4cfc9409e86d8918647d161f6cccccd1ba270e603575b8fc9f5167e58a48.svg) these solutions approach the origin as ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/e54727d514ed264e6dd30c7f4044746e6d2b4b462dc3776daecf7eb68634c358.svg)\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/317fe507f591931ea371db43b78a83b1741c427ef89dd90571f0a0030ed70c20.png)\n\nFor this particular system, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/878b11e2e3f3f3aaa6133482d483f1aa22ff420ade2a3d9533692f04c47348d1.svg)\nthus, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/e2c67900a3ba263aad1f200c892be4d755ab441e6b96ad6317e9364121f597b4.svg) is the eigenvalue that determines the long-term behavior (dominant eigenvalue).\n\nSince the dominant eigenvalue is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/413cdb74711dd235ff727690ee5fb8713e6f50cbb49d131121a40b18b0943f53.svg) solutions become parallel to the straight-line solution containing the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/ed99403d5ac94993d00ca1f9c99def2e8d3bcbddba68d8aa1c1a8651fd140e2a.svg) as they move towards the origin.\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14122747/assets/3a6d8a97c6d07c78562c73dbd1abef1b1a3c0d9f38cd14f4f9874df091492b9e.png)",
